From: Michiel Bruijn <michiel@bruijn.nu>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 08:45:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] secur32: Implement ImpersonateSecurityContext() and
 QuerySecurityContextToken() for NTLM.

Keep the token of the authenticated client in the server context of msv1_0,
pass it to the calling process through the user mode context data and expose
it through SpGetContextToken(); Negotiate forwards to the selected package.
SQL Server impersonates clients logging in with integrated security.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016s12iuoTmYVZJQsft4SbDV
---
